          "id": "Ed53q",
          "name": "Detail",
          "context": "Settings › Appearance. Inline nav-bar title. Theme: System (default), Light or Dark, kept on this iPhone only and cleared by Log Out; System follows the iPhone's setting. The choice sets the window's style, so the call screen and photo/video compose still go dark over it. Logo: Detailed draws the app icon's veil with folds and shading (design/icon/shroud-icon.svg), Simple the flat veil (shroud-icon-simple.svg); changing it also changes the home screen icon, which iOS confirms with its own alert. If iOS refuses the icon change, a red 13 pt line under the Logo footer reads “The app icon couldn’t be changed. Try again.” Rows highlight on press; the checkmark swaps with Motion.iconSwap. Switching the theme cross-fades the whole window over 0.3 s.",
